Example directory for testing object map of various containers
Uses the same containers as for the serialization tests.

This is the relevant issue from when I was testing the various 
containers by hand:
https://github.com/sstsimulator/sst-core/issues/1354

The /tests/components/CaptCrunch directory has the original tests
used to test serialization of basic types and containers. 
The /tests/components/CaptCrunchObjMap directory has bascially the 
same components, but I've #defined and/or commented out most of them
so that you can focus on just a few at a time. 

The /test/component_tests/cmd-unsignedSet-DEV.sh provides an example
test script for the unsignedSet. It does the following:
-----------------------------------------------------------
Entering interactive mode at time 0
Interactive start at 0
> cd c0
> ls
charSet/ (std::set<char, std::less<char>, std::allocator<char> >)
clockHandler/ (SST::SSTHandler2<bool, unsigned long, SST::CaptCrunchObjMap::CaptCrunchObjMap, void, &SST::CaptCrunchObjMap::CaptCrunchObjMap::clockTick>)
component_state_ = 3 (SST::BaseComponent::ComponentState)
my_info_/ ()
my_info_/ (SST::ComponentInfo*)
numClocks = 10000 (unsigned long)
numStats = 100 (unsigned long)
structSet/ (std::set<SST::CaptCrunchObjMap::CaptCrunchObjMap::__fundamentalTypeStruct, std::less<SST::CaptCrunchObjMap::CaptCrunchObjMap::__fundamentalTypeStruct>, std::allocator<SST::CaptCrunchObjMap::CaptCrunchObjMap::__fundamentalTypeStruct> >)
unsignedSet/ (std::set<unsigned int, std::less<unsigned int>, std::allocator<unsigned int> >)
> cd unsignedSet
> ls
0 = 1234 (unsigned int)
1 = 1235 (unsigned int)
----------------------------------------------------------------

It greps for correct output in the output file and will print PASS if found.
i.e.
0 = 1234
1 = 1235


